@import copy from '../../components/copy.clarus'
@import docs from '../../layouts/docs.clarus'

<docs [title]="'Lazy attach'" [path]="'/guide/lazy-attach'" [description]="'Load an island\'s code when the browser is idle, when it is visible or on first use.'">
  <h1>Lazy attach</h1>
  <p class="lead">By default an island's code loads as soon as the page does. Add <code>attach</code> to load it later.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Loads</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>attach="load"</code></td><td>as soon as the page loads (the default)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>attach="idle"</code></td><td>once the browser has nothing else to do</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>attach="visible"</code></td><td>when it scrolls into view</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>attach="interaction"</code></td><td>the first time someone clicks, types or focuses inside it</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="sample"><pre><code verbatim><comments attach="visible" [post]="post.id" /></code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <p>Nothing the visitor does is lost while the code loads: clicks, key presses, input and form submissions inside the island are held and replayed once it attaches, and a form doesn't post in the meantime. The copy buttons on this site use <code>attach="interaction"</code>.</p>
</docs>
